# Citation metadata for lsdtt3 (Citation File Format, https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo reads it when it archives a
# release.
#
# Deliberately no `version:` or `date-released:`. lsdtt3's version lives in
# CMakeLists.txt (tools/set_version.py), and a copy here would go stale; Zenodo
# takes the version and date from the release tag.
#
# The DOI below is Zenodo's CONCEPT DOI: it represents all versions and always
# resolves to the latest. Do not replace it with a single version's DOI (v0.9.2
# is 10.5281/zenodo.24110424); those go stale at the next release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lsdtt3 in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LSDTopoTools3 (lsdtt3): topographic analysis for geomorphology"
abstract: >-
  lsdtt3 is a C++17 library and set of command-line tools, with Python
  bindings and a QGIS plugin, for topographic analysis in geomorphology:
  DEM preprocessing, flow routing, channel and basin extraction, chi and
  channel-steepness analysis, hillslope and surface metrics, cosmogenic
  nuclide analysis, hydrological and landscape evolution modelling. It is a
  redesign of LSDTopoTools2.
